        "text": "So far so good. It came with two silicone holders and four extra refills for a total of six . I have five dogs but only put it on two of them right now. My Shiba Inu is very sensitive to fleas and she started scratching recently and that usually means fleas but I don't see any on her or any of the dogs so it could be mosquitoes I suppose.I had to do something in the yard and I saw the mosquitoes starting to swarm me. They have been Relentless and won't leave me alone. I grabbed my other dog's collar and carried it with me so I could finish the project I was doing and the mosquitoes left. I watched them fly away. If they hate it then great! I might have to use the refills for myself. Maybe put them in my socks or something. They smell atrocious though. The mixture smells like toilet bowl cleaner but I really don't care if it works because I don't want to give poison to my pets but I absolutely cannot have them get bit by anything.As far as I know they don't kill fleas or ticks, they just repel them so make sure you get this before going out and about and picking up fleas or ticks. If you do get fleas you're going to have to do something else to get rid of them. So far I don't think I have any in my yard but we do have wildlife coming through. I am happy to have this product for going on nature walks. Last time three ticks tried to climb up my dog's legs. Luckily I found them and pulled them off before they attached. We didn't have these collars yet.",
