        "position": 2,
        "title": "Impressed with first set, so got another. Best alternative to sprays, baths, and liquid applications",
        "text": "This was the second version of this product that I requested. The reason being, the rosemary element instead of the chamomile was used. Much better for insect repellent properties with the herbal constituent essential oils of: camphor, eucalyptol, and 1,8-cineole. So not only as a deterrent for fleas, ticks, and flies, but for lice too.This product comes in a tin for storing the extra and future monthly replacements (pic 1). Each pre-loaded medallion is individually sealed along with 2 other beads. This set has a full 6 month supply of prevention use (pic 2). The holders themselves slip onto dog collars, and eliminate the multiple neck attachments you put on your pet. I like this better because there is less chance of our dog getting caught up in brush and freaking out or getting hurt. This method of infestation protection with swapping out a bead, is now our preference. Not having our pet have an adverse reaction to any chemical applications is a high priority for her continued health. This works for her and keeps her more comfortable without being pestered by insects constantly. No horseflies either is a great bonus since we live by water.I'm very smitten with these and the product execution that created them. My only issue is I think the label on the one I received was put on by accident. Ours doesn't have the rosemary listed (pic 3), but the picture on the listing does have the ingredient (pic 4). If the citronella wasn't so overpowering, I'd maybe be able to smell and discern if it is correct in the oil inclusions. As it stands, I rated this 4 stars because of that. Hopefully this will be updated in the future to reflect proper ingredients.",
